[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1119,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 1158,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154334,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 274,
        "headingId": 1158,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Lipoblastoma-like tumour (LLT) is a benign spindle cell neoplasm of mature and immature adipocytic differentiation sharing morphological features of spindle cell lipoma, myxoid liposarcoma, and lipoblastoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:33:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1120,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 1159,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154335,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 274,
        "headingId": 1159,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8881/0 Lipoblastoma-like tumour</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:33:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1121,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 1160,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154336,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 274,
        "headingId": 1160,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>XXX</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:33:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1122,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 1161,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154337,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 274,
        "headingId": 1161,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> fibrosarcoma-like lipomatous neoplasm.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:33:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1123,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 1162,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154338,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 274,
        "headingId": 1162,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:33:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1124,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 1163,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154339,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 274,
        "headingId": 1163,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>LLT has been reported more commonly in the genital/perigenital region, but tumours involving the extremities, trunk, pelvis, and retroperitoneum have been described {37307874; 37355153; 37771086; 31622502; 32617677}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:33:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1125,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 1164,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154340,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 274,
        "headingId": 1164,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most frequently LLT presents as a swelling, cyst, or nodule that can be associated with pain or tenderness {29976943; 25929353}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:33:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1126,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 1165,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154341,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 274,
        "headingId": 1165,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>LLT is rare and occurs in both sexes, although it shows a predilection for the vulva {37355153}. Patients are often diagnosed in early to mid adulthood {37307874; 37355153}, with few reports of tumours in adolescence {12047760; 25929353} and rare cases in infancy {37355153}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:33:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1127,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 1166,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154342,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 274,
        "headingId": 1166,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:33:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1128,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 1167,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154343,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 274,
        "headingId": 1167,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Recurrent gene rearrangements, fusion events, and mutations have not been observed in LLT. Specifically, copy-number variation analysis, break-apart FISH, and next-generation sequencing have demonstrated no evidence of <em>RB1</em> loss and <em>DDIT3</em> or <em>PLAG1</em> rearrangements {37307874; 37355153; 29976943}. Genomic copy number by chromosomal microarray revealed a normal diploid profile with occasional focal gains or losses {37307874; 29976943}. An <em>IDH1</em> variant was reported in one LLT of the tongue {39925152}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:33:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1135,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 1174,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154344,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 274,
        "headingId": 1174,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>LLT forms a well-defined myxoid or gelatinous mass that is often lobulated and has a tan-yellow (fatty) cut surface. Small cysts may be present, but necrosis is not seen. Tumours have ranged from 20&nbsp;mm to 300&nbsp;mm {29976943; 37355153}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:33:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1129,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 1168,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154345,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 274,
        "headingId": 1168,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>LLT has a multinodular to multilobulated architecture that is delineated by acellular fibrous bands of varying thickness. Tumour matrix is often richly myxoid, but can be collagenous, and prominent thin-walled plexiform vasculature resembling that of myxoid liposarcoma is seen in either stromal configuration. The nodules and lobules are populated by a mixture of mature adipocytes, small univacuolated and bivacuolated lipoblasts, and cytologically bland spindle cells with fibrillary cytoplasm and blunt-ended to tapered nuclei. Lipoblasts can be sparse or plentiful and may be concentrated at the periphery of some tumour nodules or lobules. Mitoses are infrequent. Necrosis is absent {12047760; 25929353; 29976943; 37307874; 37355153; 40409687; 40205930; 30853315; 29300200}.</p>\r\n<p>LLT immunohistochemically lacks expression of RB1 or has a heterogeneous (mosaic) pattern of alternating weakly positive to negative nuclear expression {29976943; 25929353}. Desmin and/or S100 expression has been reported in as many as 60% of cases {23887155}. CD34 positivity is observed in a minor subset of LLT {25929353}. Some tumours may be weakly positive for PLAG1, DDIT3, MDM2, and CDK4 by immunohistochemistry, but they do not harbour genetic abnormalities involving their coding genes {37307874; 37355153}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:33:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1130,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 1169,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154346,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 274,
        "headingId": 1169,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Insufficient data</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:33:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1131,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 1170,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154347,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 274,
        "headingId": 1170,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:33:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1134,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 1173,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154348,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 274,
        "headingId": 1173,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> lobulated growth delineated by variably sized septa; admixture of mature adipocytes, univacuolated and/or bivacuolated lipoblasts, and bland spindle cells; variably myxoid to collagenous matrix and thin-walled plexiform vasculature.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> molecular genetic testing to exclude mimics in selected cases.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:33:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1132,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 1171,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154349,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 274,
        "headingId": 1171,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not applicable</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:33:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1133,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 1172,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154350,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 274,
        "headingId": 1172,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours infrequently recur locally, often because of resection margin involvement {25929353; 37307874; 37355153}. One myxoid tumour reported as LLT metastasized {37355153}, but distant dissemination has otherwise not been described in series of LLT.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:33:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]